III. RESULTS AND DISCUSSION
According to the results of our tertiary study, 53
systematic reviews have been performed on various R E
topics reported in 64 publications (including confe rence
papers, journal papers, theses, and technical repor ts). The
time period for the publications in our result is f rom 2006
till 2014 (Figure 1). There has been a sudden incre ase in the
number of publications since 2009 onwards. In our 6 4
resultant publications, there are 31 conference pap ers, 16
journal papers, 4 workshop papers, 4 technical repo rts, and
8 theses. We were unable to determine the type for one
publication (S40) as the full details were not avai lable
online. Out of 53 studies there are 12 Systematic M apping
Studies (S4, S6, S7, S9, S10, S12, S21, S34, S43, S 44, S45,
and S46), one Meta-Analysis (S42), and the rest are  all
Systematic Literature Reviews.

